    }
    ...
    env = new Environment(map);
    ...
    return env;
  }
  ```
  So environments created via `GameWorld.getEnvironment(IMap)` are guaranteed to have a non-null map. However, that does not cover all possible ways an `Environment` might be instantiated; nothing in the provided code enforces that every `Environment` in the system must come only from this path or with a non-null map.

Additionally, multiple methods in `Environment` itself explicitly check for `this.getMap() == null` before using it:

