- `public final void init() { ... if (this.getMap() != null) { ... } }`
- `public void load() { ... if (this.getMap() != null) { ... } }`
- `public void updateLighting() { if (this.getMap() != null) { ... } }`

These checks show that the library itself considers `getMap()` potentially null on an `Environment` instance and guards against that.

Since at the specific call site `this.environment.getMap()` there is no preceding null check on `this.environment.getMap()` and no stronger invariant shown that `this.environment` must always hold an `Environment` constructed with a non-null `IMap`, the field `this.map` can be null in principle, and thus `getMap()` can return null at this call site.
